{
  "@context": "https://doi.org/10.5063/schema/codemeta-2.0",
  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "identifier": "pollinatoR",
  "description": "Tools for estimating the contribution of insect pollinators to crop yield from pollinator-exclusion experiments (open versus caged, and related contrasts). Provides model-based average and conditional treatment effects with propagated uncertainty, uncertainty-aware dependence indices (a defensible replacement for bare ratio indices such as the Relative Interaction Index), a within-between decomposition that shields the exposure-by-treatment estimand from site-level confounders such as an unobserved genotype, a permutation guard against the spurious correlation that arises when a dependence index is regressed on a yield axis that shares a term, and structural data-integrity checks. The methods are general to open-versus-exclusion designs across crops and are not specific to any one study. Developed with support from the Grains Research and Development Corporation (GRDC project USQ2401-002RTX) and Analytics for the Australian Grains Industry (AAGI).",
  "name": "pollinatoR: Uncertainty-Aware Pollinator-Dependence Analytics for Exclusion\n    Experiments",
